<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-11-03 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>Tickets for The Program are on sale now. Check out our partners like Crossfader.com who will be featuring videos of MCs and Producers involved in The Program,&nbsp; Synchronicitylive.com who will be webcasting all 5 nights live, 90.3 KEXP who will feature groups from The Program on the week of the festival, and The Stranger who will be doing some great coverage of NW hip hop. Get tickets now, we expect all nights to sell out.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-11-03 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>Hello Friends,<br /><br />I just found some pictures from a trip to <strong>Los Angeles</strong> a few months back and I thought they may be of some interest to the Massline community.<br /><br />LA
is a city full of celebrities and you never really know who you might
meet. For example, I was just strolling around Hollywood one day when I
bumped into: <a href="http://www.channel102.net/show.php?show=79" target="_blank"><strong>DR. MIRACLES</strong></a>.<br /><br /><img src="http://img362.imageshack.us/img362/1461/dsc01384pw8.jpg" alt="" /><img alt="" /><br /><br />For those of you not familiar with Dr. Miracles, he is the star of the former Channel 102 show &ldquo;Dr. Miracles.&rdquo; And guess what??<br />
<br /><img src="http://img530.imageshack.us/img530/3640/dsc01386ik4.jpg" alt="" /><br /><strong>Oh Snap! He reps the Massline!<br /><br /></strong><em>WARNING:Dr.Miracles
if not for everyone. The show is what we call a &ldquo;guilty pleasure.&rdquo; A
very funny, guilty pleasure. Massline is not endorsing Dr.Miracles.
Dr.Miracles is endorsing Massline.</em><br /><br />On a completely unrelated note, I also bumped into actor/comedian/Blue Scholars fan <strong><a href="http://randallparkplace.com/" target="_blank">RANDALL PARK</a></strong>.<br /><br /><img alt="" /><img src="http://img225.imageshack.us/img225/4835/dsc01391un6.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />The homie Randall is one of the stars of <strong>MTV&rsquo;s <em>Wildin&rsquo; Out</em></strong> and was known as &ldquo;Randruff&rdquo; in the LA area hip-hop group <a href="http://profile.myspace.com/index.cfm?fuseaction=user.viewprofile&amp;friendid=2579951" target="_blank"><strong>ILL AGAIN</strong></a>. <br /><br />Alright everybody, I must leave you know. &quot;Cheers.&quot;<br /><br />-Hari<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-30 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>wassup people. <br /><br />big things goin down this Thursday at Neumo&#39;s.  <br /><br /><br /><br /><br />1.  THURSDAY NIGHT<br /><br />2.  BEAT BATTLE<br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br />3.  <strong><font size="10">ALL AGES</font></strong><br /><br />if you would like to go, please email us your FIRST and LAST name to the following address:<br /><br /><strong>bluescholarsevents(at)gmail.com</strong><br /><br />when i receive it, i&#39;ll put you on the list and you can come thru.<br /><br />-saba<br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-30 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><strong>Common Market - London Bridge Studio Sessions</strong><br /><br /><img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2058/1805264984_e75c4727de_o.jpg" alt="" width="424" height="281" /><br /><br />I&#39;ll be real about it. Due to an unprofessional (ie hella wack) move by some dood (ie wack mofo), Sabzi and RA Scion (bka Common Market) had only <strong>5</strong> days to re-record material for their latest LP, <em>Tobacco Road, </em>in none other than (cue blessing in disguise) the world famous London Bridge Studios. Yes, that one -- the one where Pearl Jam, Blind Melon, Soundgarden, Alice in Chains, and the world famous Nickelback (7x Plat plaque and Geo&#39;s favorite) have recorded albums defining Seattle&#39;s grunge rock sound of the early 90&#39;s (sans Nickelback of course).<br /><br />I&#39;ll admit that I was excited to visit this joint. Me and the homie Olaf had matter-of-factly just watched <em>Singles</em> on DVD (the soundtrack was recorded at LB), so I was already in that nostalgic mood. I had a feeling we&#39;d be there for a while so I brought my copy of <em>American Gangster</em> (the album and the DVD, son)...but we never ended up watching it. Also, Geo and I met up with a guy who was selling a laptop on craigslist at a local strip mall nearby and he happened to have heard of Blue Scholars. Anyway, I digress...<br /><br /><img src="http://i29.photobucket.com/albums/c271/SCIONtificrecords/Studio%20Pics/DSC_3438.jpg" alt="" width="424" height="640" /><br /><br />The studio itself, as cliche as it sounds, has an aura to it. There&#39;s a large room with a grand piano and Wurlitzer, a percussion room (where Saba, Geo, myself and Nam played with all sorts of drums and shaker instruments), a small mic booth inbetween the rooms, and a large Neve board from 1973.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2156/1804416331_87b9b92d82_o.jpg" alt="" width="424" height="976" /><br /><br />Also armed with Pro Tools, the fellas slaved away (that&#39;s racist!) for hours on end making sure songs such as &quot;Fourty Thieves&quot;, &quot;Nothing At All&quot; and &quot;Trouble Is&quot; flicked the inside of your brain in attempts to wake you up (in all sorts of ways). This is going to definitely be a different Common Market. Oh yeah, and M cooked some really good pasta.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2299/1804430465_00a9998835_o.jpg" alt="" width="424" height="281" /><br /><br />Songs sung while we were chillin: &quot;Alive&quot;, &quot;Black Hole Sun&quot;, &quot;Umbrella&quot;, &quot;Under the Bridge&quot;, &quot;No One&quot;, and of course, Nickelback&#39;s &quot;How You Remind Me&quot;. <br /><br /><img src="http://i29.photobucket.com/albums/c271/SCIONtificrecords/Studio%20Pics/DSC_3427.jpg" alt="" width="424" height="640" /><br /><br />The album will go through its final stages in November, with a release date in early 2008 (so vague, yeah?). In the meantime, you can look forward to the Blue Scholars &quot;Joe Metro&quot; EP on Nov. 6, which I also got a chance to hear....and ladies....&quot;Southbound&quot; is for <em>you</em>.<br /><br />Peace<br />daps1<br /><br />p.s. NOV 1 - BIG TUNE BEAT BATTLE - NEUMOS - SUPPORT UR BOYS SABZI AND BRAINSTORM - BE THERE! ...AND FREE DJ DV-ONE!<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> [11] <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?